**What the two boards do.** Legal (`C-NB-LEGAL`) asks *may we* with normative-source evidence, default-deny, and option veto. Risk (`C-NB-RISK`) asks *how exposed are we* with an exposure model and no permission grant. When legal is FORBIDDEN and risk is ACCEPT, the joint disposition is FORBIDDEN; the risk finding is a counterfactual appendix, not minority dissent and not irreducible disagreement.

